      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think though this would be handy, one caveat: To gain access to a users transforms, a sort of \"permission\" system should exist.\nSomething akin to a popup for the user that effectively states \"This application would like to control your transforms, Y/N\"\nTo gain control of the player, permission should be given to the app first, for sure. (Though you can have a starting area in your map of course that starts the player off by requesting permission of course)\nGoal here is simply speaking to prevent individuals from abusing this by creating troll worlds that take control of the player and make it difficult for them to teleport out.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
